usage: q04_runtime.py [-h] --phase {init,matrix,warm,drain,guard} --bundle
                      BUNDLE --state STATE --capacity CAPACITY [--name NAME]
                      [--fresh FRESH] [--fixture {native,06,07,08,09,10}]
                      [--model-cache MODEL_CACHE] [--temporal TEMPORAL]
                      [--endpoint ENDPOINT] [--bucket BUCKET]
                      [--prefix PREFIX] [--pod-namespace POD_NAMESPACE]
                      [--trial-seconds TRIAL_SECONDS] [--capacity-approved]

Q04 actual Activities/shared-storage matrix; requires a newly approved
capacity file. Only --help is a local dry run. Use prepare.py and
test_adapter.py before capacity coordination. No service scaling, historical
pauses or source deletion is built in.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --phase {init,matrix,warm,drain,guard}
  --bundle BUNDLE
  --state STATE
  --capacity CAPACITY
  --name NAME
  --fresh FRESH         Fresh matrix directory or JSON mapping fixture IDs to
                        immutable fresh case directories
  --fixture {native,06,07,08,09,10}
                        Subset for matrix only; allows separately coordinated
                        windows
  --model-cache MODEL_CACHE
  --temporal TEMPORAL
  --endpoint ENDPOINT
  --bucket BUCKET
  --prefix PREFIX
  --pod-namespace POD_NAMESPACE
  --trial-seconds TRIAL_SECONDS
  --capacity-approved
